1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:32,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,133
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,167
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:43,800
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,200
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,400
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:48,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:53,867
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,867 --> 00:00:55,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,200
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:03,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:13,233
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:22,367
<i>The criminals got away
with one bag of gold,</i>

21
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:23,900
<i> but the rest are safe now.</i>

22
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,900
<i>We had to choose Max
over the gold.</i>

23
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,500
<i>They couldn't retrieve
all of the gold.</i>

24
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,700
<i>- Paquito's son failed.
- I should've handled it!</i>

25
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,367
<i> It's easy to act tough...</i>

26
00:01:31,367 --> 00:01:32,733
<i>...when you're not
in an actual fight.</i>

27
00:01:32,733 --> 00:01:36,567
<i>I'm probably taking my acting
as Gabo's wife too far.</i>

28
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:37,900
<i> No. This is just right.</i>

29
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,900
<i>So they won't sense anything
or notice how I'm acting.</i>

30
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:43,067
<i> Pick. Ten of Swords.</i>

31
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,433
<i> Tower. Death.</i>

32
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:46,400
<i> Our daughter is dead!</i>

33
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,733
<i> Our daughter is not dead!</i>

34
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:49,667
<i> I can't take it!</i>

35
00:01:51,067 --> 00:01:52,400
[ISOBEL SOBBING] Ricardo!

36
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,567
- Ricardo!
- [DOOR SLAMS SHUT]

37
00:01:53,567 --> 00:01:57,700
Ricardo, our daughter Sam
is dead!

38
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,033
- [PINKY] Isobel, I'm so sorry.
- She's dead...

39
00:02:00,033 --> 00:02:02,433
Are you out of your mind?!

40
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:05,000
Do you seriously believe
a fortune teller?

41
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,533
Where's the proof, Isobel?

42
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:09,333
What kind of proof do you want?

43
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:11,400
The fortune teller
said so herself!

44
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:15,367
Sam was placed in a drum,
and then thrown into the water!

45
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,600
All we can do is
find her remains!

46
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,433
We won't find any corpse!

47
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:22,467
Sam is alive!

48
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:23,967
No, Ricardo!

49
00:02:23,967 --> 00:02:26,133
Use your authority as a general!

50
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:28,967
Order a search
for our daughter's corpse

51
00:02:28,967 --> 00:02:31,067
in all bodies of water, please!

52
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,967
That's never going to happen!

53
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:34,567
Isobel, you're losing your mind!

54
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:37,400
- [MAX] Mom? Dad?
- Stop!

55
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,100
Why are you shouting
at each other?

56
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,133
[TWINKLE]
They said Ma'am Sam is gone!

57
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:43,767
Yes! They said
she's dead, ma'am!

58
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:45,433
Oh, I feel so weak!

59
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:46,700
[RICARDO] It's her fault!

60
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:49,767
She's entertaining what
the fortune teller told her!

61
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,733
No, it's true!

62
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,467
She's gone! Your sister is gone!

63
00:02:54,467 --> 00:02:55,933
- Believe me!
- [MAX] Mom!

64
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:57,067
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:02:57,067 --> 00:02:59,800
We're looking for Sam,
and we'll find her.

66
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,467
So please,
don't let yourself be deceived!

67
00:03:02,467 --> 00:03:05,000
- No, it's...
- Madam Matilda is legit!

68
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,933
I proved her myself, Max!

69
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:09,067
She told me last year that
I would get rich,

70
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:10,667
and it came true!

71
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:11,833
[RICARDO] Hey, Pinky!

72
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:14,900
Predicting that a rich person
will get richer

73
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,467
is not fortune-telling!

74
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:17,767
That's a given!

75
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:19,567
That's how the world works!

76
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:22,467
You live, you laugh,
you love...

77
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,033
and then you die.

78
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:25,500
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,533
[RICARDO HUFFS]

80
00:03:27,533 --> 00:03:31,200
- [ISOBEL SOBS] I believe her.
- [PINKY CRYING]

81
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,467
[MUSIC ENDS]

82
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,833
[GABO BREATHING WEAKLY]

83
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:38,133
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

84
00:03:38,133 --> 00:03:39,167
What happened last night?

85
00:03:39,167 --> 00:03:41,467
Damn it! He has amnesia!

86
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:42,867
- Gabo, it's me. Binoy.
- Amnesia?

87
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:44,467
- Do you remember me?
- This is my chance!

88
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:46,500
Gabo. Gabo, it's me.
I'm your wife.

89
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,667
- Cut it out! That's not true.
- Tekla. Don't you remember?

90
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:49,867
You're all out of control!

91
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:50,967
- You're annoying!
- Shh!

92
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:52,867
- Tekla, stop it!
- Why?

93
00:03:52,867 --> 00:03:54,667
Keep it down!
Gloria might hear you!

94
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,967
It's better that she hears me!

95
00:03:56,967 --> 00:03:58,067
- Shh!
- Hey!

96
00:03:58,067 --> 00:04:00,533
- Just stop it!
- Yeah? Make me!

97
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:03,033
Gabo, you don't remember?

98
00:04:03,033 --> 00:04:04,700
You almost died last night!

99
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,033
Good thing we arrived.

100
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:07,467
They were about to kill you.

101
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:09,867
So we started shooting,
and the bastards ran off.

102
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:10,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,900
Luckily,
we're not sharpshooters,

104
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:14,167
so we didn't hit anyone.

105
00:04:14,167 --> 00:04:15,500
If you were sharpshooters,

106
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,933
you'd all probably be
in prison right now.

107
00:04:18,733 --> 00:04:20,467
This can only mean one thing.

108
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,533
Gloria's in danger.

109
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:29,533
The people after her
won't stop until she's dead.

110
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:32,567
That's exactly why you
should drive her away, Gabo!

111
00:04:32,567 --> 00:04:34,200
Because the people
closest to you

112
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,167
and your loved ones are
getting dragged into this!

113
00:04:36,167 --> 00:04:37,600
[TEKLA BREATHES HEAVILY]

114
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:41,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

115
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:42,900
[MUSIC ENDS]

116
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,533
[ISOBEL EXHALES, SNIFFLES]

117
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:48,100
Should I arrange a wake?

118
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:52,233
But how can I arrange a wake
without ever seeing her?

119
00:04:52,833 --> 00:04:58,100
Or will I be a mother
who cannot fully mourn

120
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,233
because her child's corpse
is missing?

121
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:03,300
[ISOBEL CRYING]

122
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:07,133
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:05:07,133 --> 00:05:09,867
[ISOBEL] She looks beautiful
in that picture.

124
00:05:10,867 --> 00:05:12,967
Let's use it for the wake.

125
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:15,267
Ma, Sam is alive.

126
00:05:15,267 --> 00:05:18,533
What can I do for you
to face reality?

127
00:05:18,533 --> 00:05:21,933
It is you and your dad...

128
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:23,967
that should face reality.

129
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:25,600
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

130
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,933
[PICTURE FRAME STAND SNAPS]

131
00:05:27,033 --> 00:05:29,567
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]
- [BREATH QUIVERING]

132
00:05:29,567 --> 00:05:31,633
My daughter, my daughter...

133
00:05:31,633 --> 00:05:32,800
My daughter...

134
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,933
[CRYING CONTINUES]

135
00:05:33,933 --> 00:05:37,233
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:38,533
[SOBS]

137
00:05:38,933 --> 00:05:40,533
Sam...

138
00:05:40,933 --> 00:05:42,733
- Sam...
- [MAX] Mom.

139
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:44,567
The fortune teller said
you're gone...

140
00:05:45,267 --> 00:05:49,033
Max, talk to your mother.

141
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:51,233
Or I might tell her
something I'll regret.

142
00:05:51,233 --> 00:05:52,300
Yes, Dad.

143
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,267
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:58,133
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

145
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,300
[TWINKLE] Sir. Sir.

146
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:07,100
- [GLASS CLINKS]
- Sir.

147
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,567
What if
the fortune teller's right?

148
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,833
He's right, sir.

149
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:15,000
Maybe we're just waiting
and searching for nothing.

150
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,600
- [GLASS THUDS]
- Stop it, the two of you.

151
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,967
I'm not like your Ma'am Isobel
who gets fooled easily.

152
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:21,200
I'm a man of proof.

153
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:23,167
As long as I don't see a body...

154
00:06:24,267 --> 00:06:25,567
...then there's no one dead.

155
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,200
But how would they find
her body

156
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,733
when it's inside a drum?!

157
00:06:31,367 --> 00:06:33,167
And they threw it into the sea!

158
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,333
[GABO] Tekla.

159
00:06:38,167 --> 00:06:39,267
I'm already in this deep.

160
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:42,000
I might as well see it through.

161
00:06:44,733 --> 00:06:47,167
I will protect Gloria.

162
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,300
Wait a minute, wait.

163
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:54,867
Do you think they know
that Gloria is here?

164
00:06:54,867 --> 00:06:56,733
I don't think so.

165
00:06:56,733 --> 00:06:58,833
All they know is
they'll get in a fight here

166
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:00,067
because we don't back down.

167
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,367
But they're brave enough
not to spare anyone.

168
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:04,367
They even have rifles, Gabo!

169
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:06,133
We have to be extra cautious.

170
00:07:06,133 --> 00:07:09,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:10,967
If that's the case...

172
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,133
...then our lives
are all in danger.

173
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:19,233
What you should do...

174
00:07:19,333 --> 00:07:22,767
...is go back to your positions
in the alleys.

175
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:26,733
Make sure no outsider
gets into Ginintuang Lupa.

176
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:29,033
- Go.
- Alright, let's go.

177
00:07:29,033 --> 00:07:31,033
- Let's go, Tekla.
- You really don't have amnesia?

178
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:34,033
Come on, you're too naughty.
Let's get out.

179
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:35,233
[TEKLA]
That could've been my chance.

180
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:37,900
[DOOR SHUTS]

181
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,233
[CRYING]

182
00:07:43,267 --> 00:07:47,100
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,367
[CRIES]

184
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,367
[ISOBEL INHALES SHARPLY]

185
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:00,967
[ISOBEL CRIES]

186
00:08:00,967 --> 00:08:02,367
- Mom?
- [ISOBEL INHALES]

187
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,767
I understand you.

188
00:08:06,367 --> 00:08:07,267
[ISOBEL INHALES]

189
00:08:08,033 --> 00:08:10,100
If you understand me...

190
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:14,000
Why don't you cry?

191
00:08:15,133 --> 00:08:16,467
Have you turned numb?

192
00:08:16,467 --> 00:08:19,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,100
[ISOBEL SNIFFLES, EXHALES]

194
00:08:24,433 --> 00:08:25,467
[MAX SIGHS]

195
00:08:26,967 --> 00:08:28,300
[ISOBEL BREATHES SHAKILY]

196
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:33,233
What I mean is, I understand
the fear you're feeling...

197
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:35,833
...because you're searching
for answers.

198
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:40,100
That's the reason you consulted
the fortune teller, right?

199
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,367
Who knew I was...

200
00:08:42,233 --> 00:08:45,300
...only holding on
to a false hope?

201
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,767
But Sam is gone.

202
00:08:48,733 --> 00:08:49,867
It hurts.

203
00:08:51,433 --> 00:08:54,133
But I must accept it.

204
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:58,333
I must tell you this, Ma.
The other day...

205
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:05,167
Someone found a corpse
near where Sam was last seen.

206
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,967
I thought...

207
00:09:07,967 --> 00:09:10,467
[ISOBEL SNIFFLES, EXHALES]

208
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:12,367
...what if that really were Sam?

209
00:09:12,367 --> 00:09:15,033
- [ISOBEL EXHALES]
- I hope not, but--

210
00:09:15,033 --> 00:09:17,100
- I hate to admit it, but...
- [ISOBEL SNIFFLES]

211
00:09:18,467 --> 00:09:19,833
[ISOBEL EXHALES]

212
00:09:19,833 --> 00:09:24,767
There was a part of me
saying, "There you go!

213
00:09:26,267 --> 00:09:28,900
You've found the answer
you're looking for.

214
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,767
Finally...

215
00:09:31,467 --> 00:09:35,500
We can end this stupid
and crazy search."

216
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,433
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

217
00:09:39,033 --> 00:09:41,533
It's only human to think that.

218
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:44,233
But you know what, Mom?

219
00:09:44,233 --> 00:09:47,233
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:09:47,233 --> 00:09:48,433
I realized...

221
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:56,167
I'd rather get tired
of searching for the truth

222
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,933
no matter how long it takes.

223
00:10:01,433 --> 00:10:02,833
[MAX EXHALES SHAKILY]

224
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:04,333
Instead of feeling...

225
00:10:06,367 --> 00:10:07,500
...relief.

226
00:10:08,267 --> 00:10:10,133
[ISOBEL BREATHES]

227
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:13,100
But that relief would mean...

228
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:17,000
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

229
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,300
...that my sister
really is gone.

230
00:10:20,433 --> 00:10:22,100
[MAX EXHALES SHAKILY]

231
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:23,333
I'll find Sam.

232
00:10:26,567 --> 00:10:30,067
- She's still alive.
- [ISOBEL CRIES]

233
00:10:30,067 --> 00:10:31,333
I'll find her.

234
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:34,300
[ISOBEL CRYING]

235
00:10:36,267 --> 00:10:37,267
Gabo.

236
00:10:38,567 --> 00:10:41,133
Are we still doing
the right thing?

237
00:10:41,133 --> 00:10:43,267
I mean, you saw it.

238
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:46,300
We might all get involved
in this mess.

239
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,267
Auntie.

240
00:10:49,133 --> 00:10:51,200
Gloria has nowhere else to go.

241
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,200
If we let her go,

242
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,267
I'm sure something bad
will happen to her.

243
00:10:57,133 --> 00:10:58,833
I'm begging you.

244
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:02,967
Let us protect Gloria.

245
00:11:02,967 --> 00:11:09,467
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,967
Don't worry, Gabo.

247
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,933
We will protect Gloria.

248
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:16,367
And we will not abandon her.

249
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:19,967
Mameng, Dante.

250
00:11:20,967 --> 00:11:27,900
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:30,533
[SAM]
<i> They're all getting involved.</i>

252
00:11:31,667 --> 00:11:33,633
<i>The situation
is still very dangerous.</i>

253
00:11:37,167 --> 00:11:39,233
<i>Those who want to kill me
won't stop</i>

254
00:11:39,233 --> 00:11:41,867
<i> until they're sure I'm dead.</i>

255
00:11:52,133 --> 00:11:53,067
Sir.

256
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:57,600
There is something
I want to tell you.

257
00:11:58,767 --> 00:12:00,467
But I hope
you won't take offense to it.

258
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,700
- It's about Ginintuang Lupa.
- What about it?

259
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:06,667
There are a lot
of potential investors

260
00:12:06,667 --> 00:12:08,433
who want to get involved
in the project.

261
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,733
Unfortunately, they know
we're not making progress.

262
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:14,467
Manny.

263
00:12:16,667 --> 00:12:18,533
What do they want me to do?

264
00:12:18,533 --> 00:12:19,800
My daughter is missing!

265
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,367
You think I'll prioritize
Ginintuang Lupa?

266
00:12:22,967 --> 00:12:26,033
Government agencies
are searching for Sam.

267
00:12:27,567 --> 00:12:30,100
Which is why I don't think we
should abandon the development.

268
00:12:31,067 --> 00:12:33,467
Yeah. You're right.

269
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:38,133
The world can't stop...

270
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:40,000
...while my daughter is missing.

271
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,100
Call our lawyer.

272
00:12:42,967 --> 00:12:45,933
Tell her we'll discuss
the demolition...

273
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,933
...of Ginintuang Lupa.

274
00:12:50,033 --> 00:12:52,733
Let me know if there are
any developments within the day.

275
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:54,033
Yes, sir.

276
00:12:54,033 --> 00:12:55,167
[ISOBEL] What's going on?

277
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,633
Um...

278
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:01,167
We'll, I'm just making sure
that we're on track

279
00:13:01,167 --> 00:13:03,733
in demolishing Ginintuang Lupa.

280
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:05,667
Business as usual?

281
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:09,533
It's as if nobody died.

282
00:13:09,533 --> 00:13:11,700
Is that how you grieve?

283
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:14,033
Or do you just not really care
about Sam?

284
00:13:14,033 --> 00:13:15,900
Isobel, I have nothing to mourn.

285
00:13:17,067 --> 00:13:19,200
Because Sam is not dead.

286
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,033
You know,
I'm just letting you believe

287
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:22,033
what you want to hear...

288
00:13:22,867 --> 00:13:25,867
even if it's wrong or foolish...

289
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,467
...because that might
calm you down.

290
00:13:28,467 --> 00:13:35,200
So ignoring what happened
to Sam is what calms you?

291
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,067
- Mom. Dad.
- [RICARDO EXHALES]

292
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:40,233
Are you fighting again?

293
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:44,700
Well, your father
keeps prioritizing his business

294
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,033
when he knows
we're going through something!

295
00:13:47,033 --> 00:13:50,133
The world can't stop
while we search for Sam!

296
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:52,133
[ISOBEL] You know, if you have
to talk to someone here,

297
00:13:52,133 --> 00:13:54,533
it's none other than your dad!

298
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:57,133
My gosh.

299
00:14:01,733 --> 00:14:04,600
Boss Mariano! What gives?

300
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:07,067
- I need to talk to your son.
- Django?

301
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:11,067
- I'll call him!
- Not on the phone.

302
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,133
Tell him to go
to the corner of your street.

303
00:14:14,133 --> 00:14:17,100
- Someone will pick him up.
- [PAQUITO]  Copy, Boss Mariano!

304
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,733
But...

305
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:21,633
Could you tell me
what this is about?

306
00:14:21,633 --> 00:14:24,767
I need your son, Paquito,
and not you.

307
00:14:24,767 --> 00:14:25,900
I'll tell him.

308
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:29,467
You know what to do.

309
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,733
Yes, sir.
I'll have him picked up. Ma'am.

310
00:14:32,867 --> 00:14:35,833
- So, what's the plan?
- I'm getting Django picked up.

311
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,133
I'll have him finish
what he started.

312
00:14:38,133 --> 00:14:39,600
What about Lucas?

313
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:43,033
I'll give Lucas another chance
to make it up to us,

314
00:14:43,033 --> 00:14:45,633
so he could prove himself.

315
00:14:45,633 --> 00:14:48,900
- He'll be in charge of Django.
- Good.

316
00:14:49,633 --> 00:14:53,100
We should make sure
that everyone new

317
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:58,833
that we let into our world
are trustworthy.

318
00:14:58,833 --> 00:15:04,500
Well, how about that NCIA agent
you trust?

319
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:05,600
Pia?

320
00:15:07,133 --> 00:15:10,667
[PHONE RINGING]

321
00:15:10,667 --> 00:15:13,867
- [BREATHING DEEPLY]
- [PHONE RINGING]

322
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,233
- Hello?
- [DEBORAH]  Pia.

323
00:15:18,233 --> 00:15:22,000
What are you doing
about my son's case?

324
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
I've been talking to someone
in the maximum security.

325
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
[PIA]  They're keeping an eye
on Victor.

326
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,167
He's not supposed to be there
to begin with!

327
00:15:30,167 --> 00:15:31,833
<i> Our agreement</i>

328
00:15:31,833 --> 00:15:35,000
was you'll find a way
to get him out, right?

329
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:36,767
I'm fixing it, ma'am.

330
00:15:36,767 --> 00:15:38,733
The next time we talk,

331
00:15:38,733 --> 00:15:41,133
you better have
something good for me.

332
00:15:42,033 --> 00:15:44,667
<i>I've been very patient
with you, Pia.</i>

333
00:15:44,667 --> 00:15:50,233
You wouldn't like it
if I lose patience with you!

334
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,900
[INHALES]

335
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:57,033
There's still no progress
until now.

336
00:15:57,033 --> 00:15:59,700
Could it be that woman's
just milking us for money?

337
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:02,700
She saw how much we could pay
just to free Victor.

338
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,100
That bastard might just
be toying with us!

339
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:08,200
Let her try.
I won't let that happen.

340
00:16:16,067 --> 00:16:17,033
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

341
00:16:19,767 --> 00:16:21,367
I've spoken to Mom.

342
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:25,367
Max, whatever it is
your mother's saying...

343
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:29,667
because of what
the fortune teller told her...

344
00:16:31,733 --> 00:16:32,767
...just keep it to yourselves.

345
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,233
But, on a more serious note,

346
00:16:37,233 --> 00:16:40,133
how are the NCIA
and the NLEA's efforts

347
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:41,633
in searching for your sister?

348
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,767
Dad, I can't answer
for the NCIA.

349
00:16:45,733 --> 00:16:47,100
But, as for the NLEA,

350
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:51,067
we've asked a lot of people
around Soriano Street.

351
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,333
But there are still
no witnesses.

352
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:55,733
No one heard the chaos?

353
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:58,100
No one saw it?

354
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:00,233
Or, perhaps,
is it that everyone there...

355
00:17:02,633 --> 00:17:05,267
...does not care
about your sister?

356
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:07,900
[RICARDO GROANING]

357
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:10,967
- [MANNY] Sir? Attorney is here.
- Oh?

358
00:17:10,967 --> 00:17:12,367
[RICARDO] Oh, attorney.

359
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,400
Thank you for coming.
Please, sit down.

360
00:17:16,133 --> 00:17:18,100
Attorney, what's the matter?
Dad?

361
00:17:18,867 --> 00:17:21,367
Well, we're going to discuss
the continuation

362
00:17:21,367 --> 00:17:23,867
of the development
in Ginintuang Lupa.

363
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:25,867
Doesn't it seem
like you're rushing this?

364
00:17:25,867 --> 00:17:27,700
Sam is still missing.

365
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:31,133
Max, we're not abandoning
the search for Sam.

366
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:34,833
But we also cannot abandon
our land.

367
00:17:34,833 --> 00:17:36,767
- [MAX SIGHS]
- So, attorney, any updates?

368
00:17:36,767 --> 00:17:41,167
Sir Ricardo, for now,
we need two things to proceed.

369
00:17:41,167 --> 00:17:45,833
First, to dissolve the TRO
against the demolition.

370
00:17:45,833 --> 00:17:49,333
And second, we need to get
the residents of Ginintuang Lupa

371
00:17:49,367 --> 00:17:52,133
to agree to our plans
through their signatures.

372
00:17:52,133 --> 00:17:54,033
[RICARDO SCOFFS]

373
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:56,300
I'm already being harassed
by those squatters,

374
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:58,500
and now I even have to ask
for their permission.

375
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,133
You know,
it will be faster and cheaper

376
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:02,033
if I just set that area on fire.

377
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:03,133
Dad.

378
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:05,033
Why not?
Who's going to stop me?

379
00:18:05,033 --> 00:18:07,233
They'll still accuse you.

380
00:18:07,233 --> 00:18:11,900
[MANNY] Sir, we need to do this
so we don't get dragged legally.

381
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:16,167
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:18:16,167 --> 00:18:17,133
Dad.

383
00:18:18,033 --> 00:18:19,300
Dad, I'll do it.

384
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:22,367
I can make the residents
of Ginintuang Lupa agree

385
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,767
to our development plans.

386
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:26,200
After all, I penetrated them
before right?

387
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:28,033
I can do this.

388
00:18:28,033 --> 00:18:30,733
Attorney, I need you
for my plan.

389
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:32,200
Max, you don't have
to do this.

390
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:35,000
- We have men we can use.
- No, but I wanna do it for you.

391
00:18:37,833 --> 00:18:38,967
I trust you.

392
00:18:40,033 --> 00:18:41,400
Thank you for helping.

393
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:46,367
Okay, so, Manny, while Max gets
the residents' signatures,

394
00:18:46,367 --> 00:18:48,067
you take care of the TRO.

395
00:18:48,067 --> 00:18:50,267
- Yes, sir.
- I'll just get ready.

396
00:18:50,267 --> 00:18:51,833
Attorney, let's talk later.

397
00:18:54,067 --> 00:18:55,033
Max.

398
00:18:56,200 --> 00:19:00,200
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:03,133
A lot of people there will
take advantage of your money,

400
00:19:03,133 --> 00:19:06,867
like disturbance fees,
relocation fees, or whatever.

401
00:19:06,867 --> 00:19:09,367
So, if necessary,
go ahead and bribe them.

402
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,867
You bribe them, but please.

403
00:19:11,867 --> 00:19:14,067
Don't let it cost me
an arm and a leg.

404
00:19:14,067 --> 00:19:15,933
They've already taken
a lot from us.

405
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:17,867
It's time we get even.

406
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:19,500
Yes, Dad.

407
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:27,433
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

408
00:19:30,767 --> 00:19:32,933
Sir, because of the shell
casings we recovered,

409
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,733
we're changing
our search strategy.

410
00:19:36,733 --> 00:19:38,767
We'll begin at First Creek

411
00:19:38,767 --> 00:19:40,767
and move outward
in all directions,

412
00:19:40,767 --> 00:19:42,733
including all bodies of water

413
00:19:42,733 --> 00:19:44,733
where Sam might have jumped.

414
00:19:44,733 --> 00:19:48,633
And we'll continue searching
in places where she could've...

415
00:19:48,633 --> 00:19:49,767
possibly come ashore.

416
00:19:49,767 --> 00:19:56,100
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

417
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,133
[HUFFS]

418
00:19:57,133 --> 00:19:58,400
[MAX] Sir.

419
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,767
I'll be requesting more men
for the task force.

420
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:03,933
[DOMINGO] Okay. You need
to cover all sectors.

421
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:05,800
The additional team is approved.

422
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,267
- Thank you, sir.
- [CLEARS THROAT]

423
00:20:07,267 --> 00:20:08,900
Excuse me.

424
00:20:08,967 --> 00:20:10,867
[MAX] <i> Everyone will start
</i> at First Creek.

425
00:20:10,867 --> 00:20:12,767
Both of you, head east to west.

426
00:20:12,767 --> 00:20:15,000
You two, go north to south.
Is that clear?

427
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:15,967
[ALL] Yes, ma'am!

428
00:20:15,967 --> 00:20:16,967
Move!

429
00:20:17,767 --> 00:20:19,300
Ma'am, what about me?

430
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:21,033
Let's meet at First Creek.

431
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,633
You're going back
to Ginintuang Lupa?

432
00:20:22,633 --> 00:20:24,733
I have a few things
to take care of for my dad.

433
00:20:25,767 --> 00:20:28,800
The world can't stop just
because Sam is missing, right?

434
00:20:30,133 --> 00:20:31,800
Besides, I need to do this
for my dad.

435
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:34,067
To take some
of his worries away.

436
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:39,067
[MAX] Attorney, do we need
to settle with every household?

437
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:40,233
Yes.

438
00:20:40,233 --> 00:20:43,167
If your father intends
to drive them all away,

439
00:20:43,167 --> 00:20:45,800
we'll need a written agreement
that they consent.

440
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,300
What's our option?

441
00:20:47,367 --> 00:20:50,900
We can have them sign
a Special Power of Attorney

442
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:54,200
so that we can deal with
their representative directly.

443
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,200
But, Attorney,

444
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,833
we can't let them know that
we're planning to evict them.

445
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:01,800
<i>Because I'm pretty sure
they won't agree.</i>

446
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,200
- A little more.
- [EXHALES DEEPLY]

447
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:04,767
Um, good day.

448
00:21:05,033 --> 00:21:06,733
[MAX] We're from an NGO,

449
00:21:06,733 --> 00:21:08,833
and we'd like to extend
a little help

450
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:11,367
to the victims
of the previous demolition

451
00:21:11,367 --> 00:21:12,833
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

452
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:15,100
- How much?
- Five thousand pesos.

453
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,333
Per household.

454
00:21:16,333 --> 00:21:18,333
Who's your representative here?

455
00:21:18,333 --> 00:21:20,400
Maybe we can just talk to them.

456
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,833
Ah, that's Rudy.

457
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:23,333
Rudy Magtibay.

458
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:25,900
His relatives were the first
to settle here.

459
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:28,167
He inherited their piece of land
over there.

460
00:21:28,167 --> 00:21:30,200
Thank you very much, ladies.

461
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,733
- We'll be on our way.
- Bye.

462
00:21:31,733 --> 00:21:32,733
Attorney.

463
00:21:32,733 --> 00:21:34,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:36,000
[CLEARS THROAT]

465
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Attorney.

466
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,400
I know the Magtibay family.

467
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:41,267
They're difficult to talk to,
especially the son.

468
00:21:41,267 --> 00:21:42,767
But it's okay.

469
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:44,800
We've got the wife on our side.

470
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:47,500
Once the residents sign the SPA,

471
00:21:48,133 --> 00:21:49,500
I'll take care of the rest.

472
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:52,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

473
00:21:52,733 --> 00:21:54,300
- [MAX] Just sign there.
- [WOMAN 1] Done.

474
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:56,433
Thank you! Wow, instant cash!

475
00:21:56,433 --> 00:21:58,367
- What's this for?
- I don't know.

476
00:21:58,367 --> 00:22:00,700
All I know is they're
giving away 5,000 pesos.

477
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:03,267
- Where should I sign?
- What's the money for?

478
00:22:03,267 --> 00:22:06,300
[WOMAN 2] Cash assistance
from an NGO for those affected

479
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:07,867
by the recent demolition.

480
00:22:07,867 --> 00:22:11,533
Just present your picture
to my staff for reference.

481
00:22:11,533 --> 00:22:13,200
Too many requirements!

482
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,867
We need to sign,
and even show ID!

483
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:17,900
Why not just hand us the money?!

484
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,967
- Yeah, that's right!
- She's got a point!

485
00:22:19,967 --> 00:22:24,067
Folks, we need to sign
the Special Power of Attorney.

486
00:22:24,067 --> 00:22:25,233
Okay, here it is.

487
00:22:25,233 --> 00:22:26,900
By signing up,

488
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:30,400
you're authorizing
Rudy Magtibay

489
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:32,400
to act as your representative

490
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:34,167
for the entire community.

491
00:22:34,167 --> 00:22:37,233
And of course,
whatever Mister Rudy decides

492
00:22:37,233 --> 00:22:41,100
from our agreement
will be binding.

493
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:42,800
Enough with the questions!

494
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,933
Sign it, and stop whining!

495
00:22:44,933 --> 00:22:46,767
Everything's in English!

496
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:49,800
They should've used Filipino
to make it clear for everyone!

497
00:22:49,833 --> 00:22:51,833
- Are you signing it or what?
- I'm signing!

498
00:22:51,833 --> 00:22:53,133
- Then do it!
- Hmph!

499
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,533
- Stay in line.
- [WOMAN 3] Thank you, ma'am.

500
00:22:55,533 --> 00:22:57,867
This has been a great help
to us, ma'am.

501
00:22:57,867 --> 00:22:59,133
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

502
00:22:59,133 --> 00:23:00,833
- Of course.
- [ROOSTER CROWING]

503
00:23:00,833 --> 00:23:02,200
You're welcome.

504
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:04,367
[MAX] <i> Attorney, let me talk
</i> to Betchay, okay?

505
00:23:04,367 --> 00:23:05,467
If that doesn't work,

506
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,467
we'll plan our next steps.

507
00:23:07,467 --> 00:23:09,100
Okay? Come on.

508
00:23:10,433 --> 00:23:11,500
Hey!

509
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:13,533
- Miss Beautiful!
- Oh, hello.

510
00:23:13,533 --> 00:23:15,533
It's been a long time!
What's up?

511
00:23:15,533 --> 00:23:18,133
Wait, where's your partner?

512
00:23:18,133 --> 00:23:20,500
Oh, he's pretty busy right now.

513
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,300
How are you doing?

514
00:23:22,333 --> 00:23:23,967
I feel great now that
we've met again.

515
00:23:23,967 --> 00:23:24,967
[BOTH GIGGLE]

516
00:23:24,967 --> 00:23:25,900
Who are you?

517
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:28,000
This is Atty. Garcia.

518
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,167
She's our lawyer at the NGO.

519
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:33,467
Whoa, things look serious now.

520
00:23:33,467 --> 00:23:35,333
- You even brought a lawyer.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

521
00:23:35,333 --> 00:23:39,333
All we want is for all of this
to be settled.

522
00:23:39,333 --> 00:23:41,633
I told you,
I'll take care of it.

523
00:23:41,633 --> 00:23:43,167
[MAX] Yes.

524
00:23:43,167 --> 00:23:47,367
What we'd really like is to meet
Mister Rudy within the day

525
00:23:47,367 --> 00:23:50,400
and have him sign
the settlement, so...

526
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:51,467
this can finally be resolved.

527
00:23:51,467 --> 00:23:53,233
Good thing I'm here,

528
00:23:53,233 --> 00:23:55,200
so I know everything
that's happening.

529
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,867
- This way.
- Sure thing.

530
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:59,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

531
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,667
[BETCHAY CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

532
00:24:00,667 --> 00:24:01,867
Miss Beautiful?

533
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:04,667
We just have a little problem.

534
00:24:04,667 --> 00:24:07,200
Last night, my husband
and I had a fight.

535
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:12,033
Now I'm not sure
what mood he's in.

536
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:17,000
He might be upset.

537
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,167
[MAX] Mmm.

538
00:24:18,167 --> 00:24:19,500
So what now, Miss Betchay?

539
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:21,900
You promised to take care of it.

540
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:23,200
You even asked money

541
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:24,867
for his hospital bills
and medication.

542
00:24:24,867 --> 00:24:26,233
I thought you just wanted
to help us.

543
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:29,600
It was such a
small amount anyway.

544
00:24:29,633 --> 00:24:31,200
We're struggling badly,

545
00:24:31,200 --> 00:24:34,400
and my husband nearly died
from being shot.

546
00:24:35,067 --> 00:24:37,200
So what are we going to do now?

547
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,600
How about this?

548
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:41,267
I'll do the talking.

549
00:24:41,267 --> 00:24:45,000
Let's just check the mood
of the folks back home.

550
00:24:46,267 --> 00:24:48,867
Let me try to talk
to them first, okay?

551
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,367
Let's go.

552
00:24:54,467 --> 00:24:59,267
Gabo, if Betchay sees your face,

553
00:24:59,267 --> 00:25:02,033
I'm sure it'll turn into
a huge mess again.

554
00:25:02,067 --> 00:25:05,567
You'll eat her tirades
for breakfast again.

555
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:08,567
[DANTE] For sure.

556
00:25:08,567 --> 00:25:12,267
I'm sure she's still mad
about last night.

557
00:25:12,267 --> 00:25:14,100
She won't leave you alone.

558
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:19,567
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

559
00:25:19,567 --> 00:25:23,233
You know, I don't know
what to do with Betchay anymore.

560
00:25:24,067 --> 00:25:25,433
I really don't know
what to do with her.

561
00:25:27,467 --> 00:25:29,533
[DANTE]
You know, Rudy, you're right.

562
00:25:30,233 --> 00:25:31,967
Betchay and Gloria have

563
00:25:31,967 --> 00:25:33,600
completely different
personalities.

564
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:35,200
That's why Gabo is lucky.

565
00:25:36,267 --> 00:25:38,100
- [MAMENG] So, Gabo...
- [DANTE CHUCKLES]

566
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:41,600
When you're looking
for a woman to marry,

567
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:46,233
make sure to find someone
like Gloria, alright?

568
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:54,933
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

569
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:15,333
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

570
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,900
Look! Miss Betchay brought
some friends!

571
00:26:19,900 --> 00:26:21,167
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

572
00:26:21,167 --> 00:26:23,500
[ESTONG] Ma, looks like
she's in a bad mood again.

573
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:25,200
So what if she's in a bad mood?

574
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:27,133
She ruined the celebration
last night!

575
00:26:27,467 --> 00:26:30,000
- She might hear you!
- I don't care!

576
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,700
I actually want her to hear me!

577
00:26:31,700 --> 00:26:33,200
That attention seeker!

578
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,467
I'll deal with you later.

579
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:35,533
[ESTONG] Ma, stop!

580
00:26:35,533 --> 00:26:36,500
Betchay.

581
00:26:37,633 --> 00:26:38,633
Who are you with?

582
00:26:39,167 --> 00:26:40,167
[BETCHAY CHUCKLES]

583
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:43,000
Some people who will help us.

584
00:26:43,033 --> 00:26:49,667
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

585
00:26:49,667 --> 00:26:50,900
[CLEARS THROAT]

586
00:26:57,567 --> 00:27:00,000
Can I talk to you?

587
00:27:04,367 --> 00:27:05,567
I-I know...

588
00:27:05,567 --> 00:27:08,100
what I did last night was wrong.

589
00:27:08,100 --> 00:27:11,567
I know that the words
I said were hurtful.

590
00:27:11,567 --> 00:27:13,367
I hope...

591
00:27:13,933 --> 00:27:15,933
...you can forgive me.

592
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:17,433
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

593
00:27:17,433 --> 00:27:19,100
[CHAIR RATTLES]

594
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:22,100
It's good that you realized
what you did was wrong!

595
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,033
I know that.

596
00:27:26,233 --> 00:27:28,667
I regretted it all night.

597
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:34,067
It was hard for me to swallow
those hurtful words I said.

598
00:27:34,433 --> 00:27:35,967
But I hope...

599
00:27:35,967 --> 00:27:38,467
I hope you can forgive me.

600
00:27:38,467 --> 00:27:42,267
What's gotten into you that
you're asking for forgiveness?

601
00:27:42,267 --> 00:27:43,600
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

602
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,700
Uh...

603
00:27:46,433 --> 00:27:49,967
There are some people outside
who want to talk to you.

604
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,467
They're from the NGO.

605
00:27:53,633 --> 00:27:56,467
You know, Rudy,
they want to settle.

606
00:27:56,467 --> 00:27:58,467
They can help us.

607
00:27:58,467 --> 00:28:00,800
[RUDY]
Betchay, what do you mean?

608
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:03,800
Rudy, they're offering
a large amount of money.

609
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:05,133
[RUDY] Betchay...

610
00:28:05,133 --> 00:28:07,733
I'll never agree
to a settlement!

611
00:28:08,133 --> 00:28:09,333
What do they think?

612
00:28:09,333 --> 00:28:12,100
That they can buy my life
with their money?

613
00:28:12,100 --> 00:28:13,100
[BETCHAY] Rudy.

614
00:28:13,333 --> 00:28:15,433
Can't we at least talk to them?

615
00:28:15,433 --> 00:28:18,567
Let's just listen
to what they have to say.

616
00:28:18,567 --> 00:28:22,333
We should let them explain
their side.

617
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,033
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

618
00:28:24,033 --> 00:28:25,367
Give them a chance, Rudy.

619
00:28:25,367 --> 00:28:26,433
Let's hear them out.

620
00:28:37,533 --> 00:28:39,333
[BETCHAY WHISPERS]
<i> Miss Beautiful, come on in!</i>

621
00:28:39,333 --> 00:28:45,300
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

622
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,667
Good morning.

623
00:28:46,667 --> 00:28:49,133
My name is Atty. Rowena Garcia.

624
00:28:57,467 --> 00:28:58,533
Good morning.

625
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:03,500
We're here again to try
to settle this

626
00:29:03,500 --> 00:29:05,700
and offer our assistance.

627
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:09,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

628
00:29:09,567 --> 00:29:11,500
[SAM] I think I know that voice.

629
00:29:22,133 --> 00:29:23,367
<i> It's Max.</i>

630
00:29:23,367 --> 00:29:24,867
<i> What is she doing here?</i>

631
00:29:24,867 --> 00:29:31,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

632
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:33,767
<i> My plan is in motion.</i>

633
00:29:33,767 --> 00:29:38,767
<i>The distrust among Team Alpha
will continue to grow.</i>

634
00:29:38,767 --> 00:29:40,767
<i> Boss Mariano called me.</i>

635
00:29:40,767 --> 00:29:42,033
<i> He'll have you picked up.</i>

636
00:29:42,033 --> 00:29:45,667
<i>Now is the right time
to set the trap for Gabo.</i>

637
00:29:45,667 --> 00:29:47,833
<i>I have to carry out
the Zafras' mission.</i>

638
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:49,100
<i> Search the whole area!</i>

639
00:29:49,100 --> 00:29:50,933
<i>I thought the NLEA people
didn't recognize you?</i>

640
00:29:50,933 --> 00:29:52,767
<i>What I can't stand is
being betrayed.</i>

641
00:29:52,767 --> 00:29:53,933
<i> What do you need from us?!</i>

642
00:29:53,933 --> 00:29:56,733
<i>- I knew you were on it!
- Wait, wait!</i>

643
00:29:57,700 --> 00:29:59,900
<i> We'll lose Ginintuang Lupa!</i>

644
00:29:59,900 --> 00:30:04,267
<i>Once Rudy signs it,
we'll be homeless!</i>

645
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:05,867
<i> They're not from an NGO!</i>

646
00:30:05,867 --> 00:30:07,033
<i> They're lying to us!</i>

647
00:30:07,033 --> 00:30:08,733
<i>And they thought
they could fool me too?</i>

648
00:30:08,733 --> 00:30:10,433
<i> They'd better be ready for me!</i>
